{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310515,"nonce":"2mGXPAtACR0z18h/6imnSwj2AsY=","title":"Frozen archive of Key Architecture Notes (symbol resolution, boxing, TAST→HIR→MIR pipeline, FMA rules, O0 pre-opt, anon objects, interface ...","message":"This archive freezes the \"Key Architecture Notes\", \"Optimization Passes\",\n\"Debugging Tips\", and \"Benchmark Verification\" sections that used to live\ninline in MEMORY.md. All still load-bearing in current code.\n\n\n- `class_fields` map: `HashMap\u003cSymbolId, Vec\u003c(InternedString, SymbolId, bool)\u003e\u003e` -- tracks (name, symbol, is_static) per class\n- `class_context_stack`: Stack of current class SymbolIds during lowering\n- `symbol_map`: Maps SymbolId -\u003e IrId (register) during MIR generation\n- Constructor's `this` is always registered as `SymbolId::from_raw(0)` -\u003e `IrId(0)`\n\n- `haxe_box_int_ptr(i64) -\u003e *u8`: Returns `DynamicValue*` -- used for Dynamic type boxing\n- `haxe_box_reference_ptr(ptr, type_id: u32) -\u003e *u8`: Boxes a pointer (class/anon) as DynamicValue -- **2 params** (ptr + type_id)\n- `haxe_array_set_i64(arr, idx, value)`: Takes raw i64 -- used for array index assignment\n- NEVER use `haxe_box_*_ptr` for array storage -- causes type_id corruption\n\n- During stdlib merge, stdlib externs REPLACE user forward-refs by NAME\n- If stdlib declares `foo(a)` (1 param) but user forward-ref is `foo(a, b)` (2 params), ALL call sites using 2 args will SIGILL\n- ALWAYS match runtime `extern \"C\" fn` signatures exactly when declaring externs in stdlib MIR builder modules\n- Bug example: `haxe_box_reference_ptr` in array.rs had 1 param, runtime has 2 → SIGILL (fixed 2026-03-05)\n\n- TAST: TypedExpressionKind::FieldAccess { object, field_symbol }\n- HIR: HirLValue::Field { object: HirExpr, field: SymbolId }\n- MIR: GEP + Store instructions\n\n- `try_extract_fmul()` in `instruction_lowering.rs` only fuses same-block fmul-\u003efadd/fsub\n- `RAYZOR_NO_FMA=1` disables FMA entirely (for debugging)\n- `RAYZOR_NO_SRA=1` disables SRA entirely (for debugging)\n- Cranelift Copy/Cast/BitCast for same types are value aliases, NOT real instructions -- cannot serve as FMA barriers\n\n**Pipeline**: Inlining(max_size=15) -\u003e DCE -\u003e SRA -\u003e CopyProp -\u003e DCE\nRuns in `run_file()` before passing module to tiered backend (which does NOT run optimization passes itself).\n\n**Architecture**: Arc-based refcounting with Copy-on-Write. Two-tier storage: Inline (sorted Vec\u003cu64\u003e) and Map (HashMap).\n**Runtime**: `runtime/src/anon_object.rs` (AnonObject, ShapeDescriptor, COW), `runtime/src/reflect.rs` (Reflect + Type API).\n**Handle**: `Box\u003cArc\u003cAnonObject\u003e\u003e` stored as `*mut u8` -- double indirection enables COW.\n**Compiler**: `lower_object_literal()` emits `rayzor_anon_new` + `rayzor_anon_set_field_by_index` per field. Field access/store intercepts check `TypeKind::Anonymous`. Shape tracking via `anonymous_shapes: BTreeMap\u003cString, u32\u003e`.\n**CRITICAL**: Anonymous field access must use the field type FROM THE ANONYMOUS STRUCT (not `expr.ty` which is Dynamic).\n**Type IDs**: TYPE_ANON_OBJECT = TypeId(6), DYNAMIC_SHAPE = u32::MAX (sentinel for Map-backed objects).\n\n**Architecture**: Fat pointer = `{obj_ptr, fn_ptr_0, fn_ptr_1, ...}` allocated per interface assignment.\n- `interface_method_names`: BTreeMap populated in `register_interface_metadata()`\n- `interface_vtables`: maps (class, interface) -\u003e method symbols, populated in `register_class_metadata()`\n- **CRITICAL ordering**: Interfaces registered before classes (two-pass type registration)\n- **Method call desugaring**: HIR desugars `d.draw()` as `Call { callee: Variable(draw_symbol), args: [d], is_method: true }` -- interface dispatch is in the Variable callee path (line ~6117)\n- `build_function_ref()` in builder.rs: Gets function pointer as i64 for vtable construction\n\n`typedef User = { var name:String; var age:Int; }` -- type-safe aliases for anonymous objects. Same runtime.\n- `resolve_through_aliases()` follows `TypeAlias` chains (max depth 10)\n- Field GET/SET resolve through aliases before checking `TypeKind::Anonymous`\n- **Key insight**: Must resolve TypeAlias-\u003eAnonymous BEFORE `is_anon` check\n\nExternal packages register via `NativePlugin` + `declare_native_methods!` macro. NO compiler core modifications needed.\n**Key design**: Instance method externs MUST accept `self` as first param. `is_mir_wrapper: false` = direct extern call.\n**Rule**: NEVER add manual MIR wrappers for external packages.\n\nDistributable package format. Binary layout: `[entry data...][TOC][toc_size: u32][version: u32][magic: \"RPKG\"]`.\nEntry kinds: NativeLib, HaxeSource, MethodTable. CLI: `rayzor rpkg pack/inspect`. Loading: `rayzor run --rpkg`.\n\n\nEliminates redundant `haxe_array_get_ptr` calls in for-in loops. Handles both stack-slot (pre-opt) and phi (post-opt) patterns.\nPipeline position: After GlobalLoadCaching, before CSE/LICM.\n\n\n- `./target/release/rayzor dump \u003cfile\u003e -O0 --function \u003cname\u003e` -- see unoptimized MIR\n- `eprintln!` in lowering functions to trace symbol resolution\n- Check `symbol_map` for expected symbols during MIR generation\n\n\n- Mandelbrot checksum: Rayzor (112798515) = Haxe C++ (112798515)\n- Memory: ~19MB with SRA (was OOM without SRA due to 875K heap allocs/frame)\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `architecture_notes_archive` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}